# Flutter Feature Rules

- Adapt to existing project architecture while maintaining clean code principles
- Use Flutter 3.x features and Material 3 design
- Implement clean architecture with Riverpod 3.x+ (`@riverpod`, `Notifier`, `AsyncNotifier`)
- Use Riverpod providers for dependency injection — no GetIt
- Implement async error handling with `AsyncValue` (`AsyncValue.guard`, `.when`)
- Use `ConsumerWidget` / `ConsumerStatefulWidget` for reactive UI
- Use `ref.listen` for side effects (navigation, snackbars)
- Implement proper routing using GoRouter
- Use proper form validation
- Use proper localization techniques (`lib/l10n/`)

## Provider placement

- `lib/core/providers/` — app-wide DI (HTTP client, config, shared services)
- `lib/features/<name>/data/providers/` — repository and data-source providers
- `lib/features/<name>/presentation/providers/` — UI state (`Notifier`, `AsyncNotifier`)

